Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:06:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: played-in OL team context, college profiles for
 every projected player
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OL grades pipeline (src/nflverse/ol_grades_pipeline.py)
- The 15% team blend stamped the POOLED multi-season team percentile on every
  lineman on the latest roster — so a starter who missed most of a bad season
  (Slater, 42% of 2025 snaps) wore all of it, and a free-agent signing inherited
  his new team's history on day one. player_team_context() now builds the unit
  result each lineman actually played in: per team-season percentiles (ranked
  within season), weighted by his snap share that season and the same 0.45^age
  recency the snap prior uses, plus an exposure term (share of a starter's
  workload over his window). blend_phase_grades() uses that context at
  TEAM_BLEND × exposure; a player with no snap record falls back to the pooled
  roster number as before. What entered the blend is reported as
  team_ctx_pass_pctile / team_ctx_run_pctile / team_ctx_exposure and carried
  through nflverse.py and tools/refresh_ol_seed.py into ol_players.
  Slater pass 63.2 → 67.8 (exposure 0.45, ctx 39 vs pooled 25).

College profiles (src/cfb/)
- profiles.build_all(): every projected skill player drafted since 2015 is
  bucketed by rookie year (link.class_pools / draft_class_of from years_exp or
  metadata.rookie_year), linked against the college rosters of his own years
  (link.build_class_link_map, espn_ids from both his class year and the current
  roster), scored through the same production tables, and ranked against the one
  2018–(current-1) reference pool so percentiles mean the same for everyone.
  Each profile carries its draft class; the card panel shows it.
- cfbfastr.build() tolerates seasons cfbfastR never published (pre-2014).
  Practical coverage: full from the 2018 class, partial 2017, none before —
  earlier play-by-play has no player ids.
- link._cache_remote() falls back to raw.githubusercontent.com when a proxy
  refuses github.com/.../raw/ redirects.
- build_seed.py passes the projected pool; tools/refresh_cfb_seed.py rebuilds
  just this block into an existing seed (same pattern as refresh_ol_seed.py).

Tests: test_ol_pipeline (played-in context + exposure scaling, snap-weighted
aggregation), test_cfb_classes (class bucketing).
